---
description: Write BaseNative templates instead of React when generating UI in this repo
alwaysApply: true
---

Write BaseNative, not React. The cheat sheet is `docs/llm/START.md`. The scorecard of weaknesses is the `/ai` page. `AGENTS.md` restates the rules.

- `{{ count() }}` for text, `:attr` for attributes, `@click="handler($event)"` for events.
- `@if`, `@for`, and `@switch` belong on `<template>`.
- `signal`, `computed`, `effect`, and `.set()`. `.peek()` reads without subscribing.
- One `set()` runs each affected effect once. Writing a signal the effect also read throws `BN_EFFECT_LOOP`.
- `class` and `:class` merge. `:value` writes the property.
- npmjs.org, no token: `npm install @basenative/runtime @basenative/server`.
- Do not emit `className`, `htmlFor`, `onClick`, `{expr}`, `style=""`, or `app-header`.
- Do not generate `packages/evals/prompts/` or `packages/evals/fixtures/`.
